# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the one required value. See RUN.md.
#
# Everything below the first two blocks is COMMENTED OUT and optional — it is
# here to document what exists, not to be filled in for a local run.

# ── required ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
#   Your own key, from https://console.anthropic.com/. Every lesson, grade and
#   plan needs it, so the backend REFUSES TO START without one rather than
#   failing later on the first request that reaches a model.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ── required for a local http run ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# CODEONBOARD_COOKIE_SECURE
#   Leave this at 0 when running on http://localhost. It decides whether the
#   session cookie carries `Secure`, which makes it https-only.
#
#   The DEFAULT IS ON, and that direction is deliberate: a missing flag in
#   production means a session cookie sent in clear, so a wrong default should
#   fail visibly on plain http rather than silently over the internet.
CODEONBOARD_COOKIE_SECURE=0

# ── authentication, optional (multi-user M2) ─────────────────────────────────
#
# CODEONBOARD_TRUST_PROXY
#   Honour `X-Forwarded-For` when deciding which IP to rate-limit. Leave unset
#   unless a reverse proxy actually sets it — a header the client controls is
#   otherwise a throttle bypass, since an attacker would simply vary it.
# CODEONBOARD_TRUST_PROXY=1

# ── Google sign-in (multi-user M6) ───────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Unset means the button is hidden and /auth/google/start redirects to
# /login?error=google_not_configured — the feature is absent rather than
# half-working. (It answered 503 with a JSON body once; that route is only ever a
# full browser navigation, so an error there has to be something a person can
# read on a page.)
#
# Redirect URI to register with Google, for local development:
#   http://localhost:8000/auth/google/callback
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
#
# CODEONBOARD_SECRET_KEY
#   Signs the short-lived cookie that carries `state` and `nonce` across the
#   Google redirect. Without it a per-process random value is used, so flows do
#   not survive a restart. REQUIRED in production — M8's startup check enforces
#   that; optional locally so a feature most runs never touch does not block
#   development.
# CODEONBOARD_SECRET_KEY=

# ── frontend ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# API_ORIGIN (read by the Next.js SERVER, in frontend/next.config.ts)
#   Where /api/* is proxied to. Replaces NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL, which was baked
#   into the browser bundle at build time — this one is read per request and
#   never reaches the client, so the API's address stops being public.
#   Defaults to http://localhost:8000.
# API_ORIGIN=http://localhost:8000

# ── production (multi-user M8) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# CODEONBOARD_ENV=production makes the startup check REFUSE to serve on an
# insecure setting rather than warn about it: insecure cookies, a missing
# signing key, a leftover localhost origin, or half-configured Google. Every one
# of those works perfectly until it matters, which is exactly why a log line is
# not enough.
# CODEONBOARD_ENV=production


# CODEONBOARD_TUTOR
#
# The Tutor: a contextual assistant in the same pane the source uses.
# DEFAULT 1 — you do not need to set this. Set it to 0 to turn the Tutor off.
#
# Read as "not explicitly 0", so unset, 1, or anything unrecognised all mean ON.
# Only a literal 0 disables it. That direction is deliberate: a typo in an
# environment variable should not silently remove a feature.
#
# On, it serves five routes under /session/{id}/tutor and the frontend draws a
# CHAT control beside Show source. Off, those routes answer 404 and no Tutor code
# runs.
#
# The flag gates BEHAVIOUR, never STORAGE. A conversation written with it on
# survives it being turned off, and comes back exactly when it is turned on again
# — see backend/learning/flags.py.
#
# THE DEFAULT WAS 0 UNTIL NOW, AND THE REASON IS WORTH KNOWING RATHER THAN
# DELETING. docs/planning/phases/evidence/tutor/ measures 1 answer leak in 30
# adversarial SCAFFOLD prompts against a stated gate of 0, and tutor.md T8 made a
# green Eval 1 the condition for defaulting on. That gate is still not met; the
# default was changed by decision so that a fresh clone runs the whole product.
# The architecture still removes the cheap leak — a ScaffoldContext has no field
# that can hold the answer — so the residual is a model reasoning its way there
# from source it legitimately holds.
#
# TO TURN IT OFF you must set BOTH halves, because they are read in different
# processes at different times:
#   .env                  CODEONBOARD_TUTOR=0        (routes, at request time)
#   frontend/.env.local   NEXT_PUBLIC_CODEONBOARD_TUTOR=0  (control, at BUILD time)
# The frontend one needs a restart of `npm run dev`, because Next inlines
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* into the bundle. Setting only the backend half leaves a CHAT
# control on screen that reports a failure on every turn.
# CODEONBOARD_TUTOR=0
